   "en": "«GEMARA:» The Gemara asks: «But didn’t you say in the first clause» of the mishna that «one may not move» one’s possessions «at all,» even from one house to another? How is it that the mishna then permits moving objects from one courtyard to another in the second clause? «Abaye said» in explanation: «In the latter clause we come to» the case of moving objects from «the house in his courtyard» to that same courtyard."
